  "details": "Update: I didn't have this problem using VRchat today. I guess it's been fixed?\n\nLooking at Task Manager, I see that every second, VR Chat continues to use more RAM. RAM usage keeps building higher and higher until it gets to 100% (or at least 98%) of my 16 GB of RAM. At which point, the game freezes and the screen goes black. I've no choice but to kill the process and start the game over again.\nI'm using Oculus Rift CV1 with Windows 10 (updated to latest version). Also latest version of VR Chat, as of this writing. Clearing the cache didn't help. I read of some trick to go to 2 worlds in a row to free resources. That didn't work either. Memory leak starts as soon as I start the game. Even in my home world or private instance worlds with no one else. Just sitting there doing nothing, with nobody, and I see the memory usage constantly climbing. Can this be fixed, please??",
